   "### development-autonomy-conflict-coordination\n\nTask: ACC-12\n\nSource requirement: policy/development/autonomy-and-conflict-coordination\n\nAcceptance: Operative accounting-related contracts, tooling and coordination must allow authorized ordinary development without task-count, failed-attempt allowance, preparation-only stage or discretionary per-run permission prerequisites. Managers continue independently within standing goals while coordinating actual conflicting writers and incompatible interfaces. Preserve the coordinator's independent acceptance/integration role and historical attempts; never retry, transfer or route around denied/restricted actions. Removal of a project quota does not grant new access or operation authority. For governed integration, Bind the complete integration base/commit/tree immediately before integration. Later lifecycle metadata additionally binds immutable ledger source commit/tree and workstream ID through the governed-composition path in docs/workstream-governance.md. The source tuple must resolve exactly, descend from the integration base and be an ancestor of the integration commit. Independent review and CI cover the full integration tuple and exact permitted metadata delta; source evidence alone does not cover metadata. Only the existing active shard and canonical manifest may differ in that metadata lane; changes outside it require a new source freeze and affected-input review. These requirements do not gate ordinary edits or focused tests.\n\nNegative evidence: Reject policy/tool changes that reintroduce those ordinary-development quotas, impose migration/admission proofs before an ordinary edit or focused test, ignore a genuine writer/interface conflict, confer author acceptance, or use a different actor/endpoint to replay a denied action. Refuse substitution of the immutable source tuple for the complete integration tuple, missing source/workstream identity, unreviewed metadata deltas, or source/tooling/documentation/policy changes routed through the metadata lane.\n\nOutputs: Exact operative policy/tool source review and focused allowed/refused coordination fixtures or source-bound decision records distinguishing ordinary development, real conflict and denied-action cases. Missing execution evidence is recorded, not invented. Record both distinct identity tuples, workstream ID, exact changed metadata paths and manifest/shard/aggregate hashes, full-tuple independent review and CI receipts, and the actual clean named integration worktree capture.\n\nDependencies: Standing AGENTS decisions apply immediately; current writer/interface ownership and coordinator authority. This criterion has no dependency on completing ACC-12 before ordinary work proceeds.\n",
