   "### development-exact-candidate-admission\n\nTask: ACC-12\n\nSource requirement: policy/development/exact-candidate-admission\n\nAcceptance: Governed candidate integration eligibility binds exact base/candidate commit and tree, clean named worktree, owned paths, governing contracts, positive/negative fixtures, stable diagnostics, successful scoped validation, independent acceptance, residual host boundaries and coordinator disposition. Bind the complete integration base/commit/tree immediately before integration. Later lifecycle metadata additionally binds immutable ledger source commit/tree and workstream ID through the governed-composition path in docs/workstream-governance.md. The source tuple must resolve exactly, descend from the integration base and be an ancestor of the integration commit. Independent review and CI cover the full integration tuple and exact permitted metadata delta; source evidence alone does not cover metadata. Only the existing active shard and canonical manifest may differ in that metadata lane; changes outside it require a new source freeze and affected-input review. Refuse dirty/detached, missing/divergent base, identity mismatch, held/rejected/superseded/abandoned dependencies and unsupported credit. Compare ancestry and tree identity; already-identical/tree-equivalent work is not merged or replayed again. These admission requirements are not ordinary edit/test prerequisites.\n\nNegative evidence: Refuse stale or forged tuples, dirty/detached worktrees, owner/path conflicts, missing or self-authored acceptance, missing negative/diagnostic evidence, inadmissible dependencies and repeat integration of equivalent trees. Refuse substitution of the immutable source tuple for the complete integration tuple, missing source/workstream identity, unreviewed metadata deltas, or source/tooling/documentation/policy changes routed through the metadata lane. A structural validator pass or self-audit does not grant semantic acceptance, release or self-hosting authority.\n\nOutputs: Exact governed preflight/ledger input and refusal/conformance records, independent acceptance and coordinator integration disposition with scoped nonclaims; ordinary-development cases remain separately legal under standing authority. Record both distinct identity tuples, workstream ID, exact changed metadata paths and manifest/shard/aggregate hashes, full-tuple independent review and CI receipts, and the actual clean named integration worktree capture.\n\nDependencies: Applicable workstream governance/ledger contracts and exact immutable candidate evidence at integration time; no admission replay or live integration is performed by this mapping.\n",
